        <mxCell id="header-sub" value="&lt;span style=&quot;font-variant-ligatures:none&quot;&gt;&lt;font color=&quot;#e2e8f0&quot; style=&quot;font-size:13px&quot;&gt;Where does a model call end up, what limits it, and how does it fall back to the homelab GPU?&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;Scope: Gemini API free tier through its OpenAI-compatible endpoint, Ollama on the homelab RTX 5080 over WireGuard, proposal of 2026-10-23 · drawn in full: what the proposal adds (IA-1) · faded: what already runs&lt;br&gt;Out of scope: the gateway&amp;#39;s filters (AI gateway internals) · the homelab cluster&amp;#39;s own platform · the Gateway API Inference Extension, useful only with several GPU replicas&lt;br&gt;Assumed: one Google Cloud project with one API key; the jwt filter copies the data_level claim into the header x-cnp-data (claimToHeaders)&lt;br&gt;v0.1 · source: cnp-docs/architecture/cnp · ai.google.dev (rate limits, Gemini API additional terms)&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontFamily=JetBrains Mono,Noto Sans Mono,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace;fontSize=11;fontColor=#94a3b8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
